  "body": "f2839722e1b3dc56368c32fd5808f172f3ea3289 changed the _initialInsertion_ conditional such that\r\n```js\r\nf = document.createElement(\"iframe\");\r\nf.src = \"...\";\r\ndocument.body.append(f)\r\n```\r\ndoesn't end up triggering the navigation algorithm because _initialInsertion_ will be true.\r\n\r\nWould this be as simple as reinstating the `src` attribute check that was removed there? (It's not entirely clear why that was removed.)\r\n\r\ncc @domenic @ytausky ",
